### Sign in — POST /api/v1/session
# Opens a session. The body is exactly what the Telegram Login Widget hands the page, hash included; paste a
# real payload rather than editing these fields, since the hash covers every one of them. What it answers and
# refuses: ../../contracts/in/web-session-api.md

@host = http://localhost:1000
# Set from the XSRF-TOKEN cookie current-session.http returns; every write needs it.
@csrfToken = paste-the-XSRF-TOKEN-cookie-value-here

### Open a session.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/session
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: XSRF-TOKEN={{csrfToken}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "id": "123456789",
  "auth_date": "1700000000",
  "hash": "the-widget's-hash-over-every-other-field"
}
